    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0571" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg499"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wallace to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 13, 1882</date>.
                        (Received Feb. 6.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of a note received from the Porte upon the subject of the new regulations
                    pertaining to the importation of alcohol. The paper is accompanied with the
                    report referred to therein as from the administration of the six contributions,
                    of which a translation is also herewith inclosed.</p>
                <p>In the same connection I have the further honor of submitting for your
                    consideration a copy of the reply which I thought best to make to the note above
                    mentioned.</p>
                <p>Hoping that it will also meet your approval, I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>LEW. WALLACE.</signed></closer>




